WEBVTT

00:11:28.516 --> 00:11:30.316
But that other question about, well,

00:11:30.356 --> 00:11:33.356
what can I do differently to be ready
for that next opportunity,

00:11:33.396 --> 00:11:35.036
that's a really critical question.

00:11:35.036 --> 00:11:36.956
Depending on the answer you get to that,

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:40.476
you can say, well, is there someone
that you can assign to me,

00:11:40.516 --> 00:11:42.236
a coach if I need one,

00:11:42.236 --> 00:11:44.956
or some other person
who can help me, you know,

00:11:44.956 --> 00:11:46.516
in this journey that I'm on,

00:11:46.556 --> 00:11:50.956
because I really would like to be able
to optimize my contributions.

00:11:50.996 --> 00:11:52.556
And I know that you can help me.

00:11:52.556 --> 00:11:55.756
DP: I think we have to get more
comfortable advocating for ourselves

00:11:55.756 --> 00:11:58.756
and finding ways that really allow
us to gain more information.

00:11:58.756 --> 00:11:59.956
Because you're right.

00:11:59.996 --> 00:12:02.196
The other data that I found
throughout the book